# Three Vertical Lines

Three Vertical Lines is a simple ISF generator for VDMX6 Plus.

It creates three vertical white lines that extend from the top to the bottom of the screen on a transparent background.
Each line can be controlled independently inside VDMX.

## Controls

Each line has two parameters:
- Line Position – moves the line horizontally from left to right
- Line Width – changes the thickness of the line

Additional controls:
- Soft Edge – softens the line edges
- Opacity – controls the overall transparency

All parameters can be mapped to VDMX sliders, MIDI, OSC, LFOs, or audio-reactive controls.

## Installation

Copy the file:
Three_Vertical_Lines.fs

to:
~/Library/Graphics/ISF/

If the ISF folder does not exist, create it.
Then restart VDMX.

The generator should appear in the ISF Sources / Generators section.
You can also drag the .fs file directly into a VDMX Media Bin.
